Blackdrift: turn off crash reporting to Mozilla.

Why: upstream Focus sends crash reports to Mozilla Socorro (and to Sentry
when a .sentry_token exists at build time). After a crash it prompts the
user, and the tab-crash screen has a pre-ticked "send crash report" box.
Blackdrift sends no data to Mozilla, so:

- the CrashReporter gets no upload services and enabled = false, so it
  stores no crash in its database and never prompts for or uploads a
  report, for uncaught exceptions and for Gecko crashes alike. Caught
  exceptions submitted by Nimbus or application-services go to an empty
  service list. The Glean crash service stays in telemetryServices only
  to satisfy CrashReporter's "at least one service" check; Glean upload
  is off (0100).
- Gecko itself still writes a minidump and a .extra file (with the page
  URL) into files/mozilla/Crash Reports/pending/ when a process crashes:
  GeckoView needs the dump to report a content crash as a crash and show
  the tab-crash screen. This patch does not touch those files; 0106
  deletes them on start, after a tab crash and on erase.
- the tab-crash screen still offers "Close tab" to recover, but hides the
  "send crash report" box and leaves it unticked.
- Settings > About no longer lists "Crashes". With the reporter disabled
  no crash is ever stored, so the list would always be empty, and with no
  services it has no report links. about:crashes still opens it (empty).

Uncaught exceptions still reach the default Android handler, so the
platform's own crash handling is unchanged.

Cut against: mozilla-firefox/firefox@6181e6b5f28a8fbae1d5c3ef6f6626b5a2180213 (Firefox 159.0.1).

diff --git a/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/Components.kt b/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/Components.kt
index cc1b39d..4897771 100644
--- a/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/Components.kt
+++ b/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/Components.kt
@@ -375,7 +375,8 @@ private fun createCrashReporter(context: Context): CrashReporter {
 
     return CrashReporter(
         context = context,
-        services = services,
+        // Blackdrift: no crash upload service (Socorro/Sentry); reports never leave the device.
+        services = emptyList(),
         telemetryServices =
             listOf(
                 GleanCrashReporterService(
@@ -390,8 +391,8 @@ private fun createCrashReporter(context: Context): CrashReporter {
             ),
         promptConfiguration =
             CrashReporter.PromptConfiguration(appName = context.resources.getString(R.string.app_name)),
-        shouldPrompt = CrashReporter.Prompt.ALWAYS,
-        enabled = true,
+        shouldPrompt = CrashReporter.Prompt.NEVER,
+        enabled = false, // Blackdrift: crash reporting is off.
         nonFatalCrashIntent = pendingIntent,
     )
 }
